Since you already have Minikube + Helm running, use the kube-prometheus-stack Helm chart.

Step 1: Create Namespace
Shell
kubectl create namespace monitoring

Verify:

Shell
kubectl get ns
Step 2: Add Helm Repository
Shell
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts

Update:

Shell
helm repo update
Step 3: Install Prometheus + Grafana
Shell
helm install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
-n monitoring

This installs:

Prometheus
Grafana
Alertmanager
kube-state-metrics
Node Exporter
Prometheus Operator
Step 4: Check Installation
Shell
kubectl get pods -n monitoring

Wait until all pods become:

Plain Text
Running

Example:

Plain Text
monitoring-grafana
monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus
monitoring-alertmanager
monitoring-kube-state-metrics
Step 5: Check Services
Shell
kubectl get svc -n monitoring

Expected:

Plain Text
monitoring-grafana
monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus
Step 6: Access Grafana

Port forward:

Shell
kubectl port-forward -n monitoring svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80 --address 0.0.0.0
 

Because you're using GitHub Codespaces:

Open PORTS tab.
Find port 3000.
Set visibility to Public.
Open Browser.
Step 7: Get Grafana Password
Shell
kubectl get secret -n monitoring monitoring-grafana \
-o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 -d && echo

Username:

Plain Text
admin

Password:

Plain Text
(output from command)
Step 8: Access Prometheus

Port forward:

Shell
kubectl port-forward -n monitoring \
svc/monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus 9090:9090 --address 0.0.0.0

Open port 9090 from the Codespaces PORTS tab.

Step 9: Verify Helm Deployment
Shell
helm list -n monitoring
 

Expected:

Plain Text
NAME NAMESPACE
monitoring monitoring
Useful Verification Commands
Shell
kubectl get pods -n monitoring
Shell
kubectl get svc -n monitoring
Shell
kubectl get all -n monitoring
Shell
helm list -n monitoring
Uninstall Later
Shell
helm uninstall monitoring -n monitoring

Delete namespace:

Shell
kubectl delete namespace monitoring

